            <ArticleTitle>Clinical evaluation of low back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>370-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To properly diagnose and treat low back pain, a thorough history and physical examination are the cornerstones. The most important diagnoses for the physician to be aware of are cauda equina syndrome, back strain, herniated disc, stenosis, and spondylolisthesis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
